5. Quick fixes (Apple's built-in model; nothing is downloaded)
Quick fixes use the on-device model that is part of macOS, under Apple's terms, through the small helper scripts/rewriter/apple/onionskin-fm, which
Onionskin builds from its own source (scripts/rewriter/apple/main.swift, MIT, like the rest of Onionskin) and ships in the zip. No model is shipped or downloaded.

6. The look of the web app: look inspired by Solid Glass by DeepLethe (MIT). Some pane, edge and shadow values in web/src/tokens.css are closely
adapted from it; no file of it is shipped.

Playwright (Apache-2.0) and Vite (MIT) are development dependencies used by the tests and the build; they are not shipped.

3. Test fixtures

`test/fixtures/engine/sample.docx`, `sample.xlsx` and `sample.pptx` are the sample documents of the office-engine fork's playground (MIT, see 2), copied unchanged; they were written with python-docx, openpyxl and python-pptx. Real Office files used by some tests are Apache POI test data (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/apache/poi), downloaded on demand by `scripts/fetch-fixtures.mjs` into the gitignored `test/fixtures/cache/` and never committed.
